WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.807
Welcome to Module 7, Advanced Python Techniques.

00:00:06.692 --> 00:00:13.495
Up to this point, we have spent a lot of time building a strong foundation in Python.

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:22.095
We have worked with variables, conditions, loops, functions, data structures, and ways to organize our code.

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:23.328
In this module,

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:30.628
we are going to take some of those ideas and look at more compact and more powerful ways to write

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:40.350
Python. You will see techniques such as list comprehensions, lambda functions, and generators.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:44.340
We will also spend some time on debugging and code efficiency.

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:49.530
I want to emphasize something from the beginning.

00:00:49.861 --> 00:00:55.173
Advanced Python does not necessarily mean writing the shortest code possible.

00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:59.893
Short code can sometimes become difficult to understand.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:05.943
Our goal is to write code that is clear, useful, and appropriate for the problem we are solving.

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:14.794
These techniques are especially helpful in analytics because we often need to filter values, transform data,

00:01:15.233 --> 00:01:21.480
sort records, or process large collections. As we move through the examples,

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:28.030
try to focus less on memorizing the syntax and more on understanding what each technique is helping us accomplish.
